 {"author_id": "733647469305864195", "created_at": "2026-10-30T05:48:20.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116044513148100795"], "id": "2116044513148100795", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 6, "impression_count": 6645, "like_count": 21, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 6, "retweet_count": 3}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2115887585335693422", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "1.5 pp of the q3 GDP increase v q2 was inventories.  Smooth out the q2 drop and inventories are stil contributing a pp over q2 and q3.    Take that out and q3 growth is solid but not remarkable https://t.co/FraEezWMT6 https://t.co/9YmTN8aRt3", "url": "https://x.com/Brad_Setser/status/2116044513148100795"}, {"author_id": "733647469305864195", "created_at": "2026-10-30T04:37:46.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116026752501985618"], "id": "2116026752501985618", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 8, "impression_count": 8373, "like_count": 37, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 4, "retweet_count": 7}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2115669192964001884", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "Nominal appreciation against dollar (and this year v EUR) is important -- it has prompted some big changes in settlement/ flows\n\nBut the broad real CNY is only back to where it was at the time of Trump's election.   The gap v trend (the \"krugman\" variable) is bigger.  \n\n1/2 https://t.co/ZvezDQz5sD https://t.co/NP2TtGCEE2", "url": "https://x.com/Brad_Setser/status/2116026752501985618"}, {"author_id": "733647469305864195", "created_at": "2026-10-30T03:21:40.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116007602643677320"], "id": "2116007602643677320", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 30, "impression_count": 20932, "like_count": 153, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 19, "retweet_count": 14}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2115916578399371316", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "Well, it could also happen if China allowed the RMB to appreciate, creating standard economic incentives to invest in the US not China to supply the US market -- and incentives for China to resume importing ...\n\n1/2 https://t.co/qMepRm1gnd", "url": "https://x.com/Brad_Setser/status/2116007602643677320"}, {"author_id": "702235316812275712", "created_at": "2026-10-30T03:10:42.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116004842355499325"], "id": "2116004842355499325", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 9, "impression_count": 9435, "like_count": 19, "quote_count": 2, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 3}, "text": "A thread of favorite Patrick Stewart TNG moments:\n\n1/ the epic of Gilgamesh (“Darmok”)\n\nhttps://t.co/k43yAD6bzD via @YouTube", "url": "https://x.com/EconBerger/status/2116004842355499325"}, {"author_id": "702235316812275712", "created_at": "2026-10-30T01:09:32.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115974350260314136"], "id": "2115974350260314136", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 4, "impression_count": 2484, "like_count": 19, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 2, "retweet_count": 2}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2114770944753545284", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "The data release we've all been waiting for - the Q3/September ECI - comes out Friday at 830 AM ET/530 AM PT.\n\nCome for the bad news about wage growth, stay for the bad news about employer health insurance contributions https://t.co/ESxP8wurXx", "url": "https://x.com/EconBerger/status/2115974350260314136"}, {"author_id": "3512101", "created_at": "2026-10-30T00:53:31.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115970319395459218"], "id": "2115970319395459218", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 5, "impression_count": 6055, "like_count": 13, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 5}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2115924940415275345", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "“And, reported here for the first time, officials in the executive office of the president and the National Security Council have discussed making a national security determination on cellular IoT modules, which connect devices to cellular networks, that could lead to their https: